WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.356 --> 00:00:18.621
The next day, Heidi made a suggestion: "Clara, I can read aloud to you every day, just as

2
00:00:18.741 --> 00:00:20.121
I did for Grandmamma."

3
00:00:21.061 --> 00:00:25.282
Clara agreed, and Heidi started reading with her usual enthusiasm.

4
00:00:26.683 --> 00:00:30.444
But Heidi had hardly begun when she cried out, "Oh no!

5
00:00:31.132 --> 00:00:32.512
Then Grannie is dead!"

6
00:00:32.933 --> 00:00:34.073
and burst into tears.

7
00:00:35.053 --> 00:00:37.094
The story was about a dying grandmother.

8
00:00:38.054 --> 00:00:43.075
It seemed so real to her that Heidi could not stop thinking that it was Peter's grandmother who

9
00:00:43.115 --> 00:00:43.636
had died.

10
00:00:47.277 --> 00:00:47.937
is dead.

11
00:00:48.497 --> 00:00:50.298
I shall never see her again.

12
00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:56.039
She never had the chance to eat one white roll," Heidi sobbed.

13
00:00:57.019 --> 00:01:01.366
Clara explained over and over that the story was about a different grandmother.

14
00:01:02.187 --> 00:01:08.092
But even when Heidi understood that it was only a story and not real, she couldn't stop weeping.

15
00:01:09.633 --> 00:01:13.137
Fraulein came into the room and Clara explained what had happened.

16
00:01:14.157 --> 00:01:17.621
As Heidi continued to weep, Fraulein became impatient.

17
00:01:17.641 --> 00:01:21.004
"Now, Heidi, that is enough!"

18
00:01:21.664 --> 00:01:22.165
she said.

19
00:01:22.185 --> 00:01:28.721
"If you act like this again while you are reading, I will take your book away and never

20
00:01:28.761 --> 00:01:29.761
let you have it again!"

21
00:01:31.361 --> 00:01:33.642
Fraulein's words had an immediate effect.

22
00:01:34.522 --> 00:01:36.103
Heidi turned pale with fear.

23
00:01:37.043 --> 00:01:38.603
The book was Heidi's one treasure.

24
00:01:39.564 --> 00:01:42.124
She quickly dried her eyes and swallowed her sobs.

25
00:01:42.945 --> 00:01:47.866
Heidi never let herself cry out loud again, but she often had to struggle to keep back her

26
00:01:47.926 --> 00:01:54.208
tears. As the weeks passed, Heidi battled silently with her terrible homesickness.

27
00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:58.802
She would sit in a corner of her lonely room until Clara sent for her.

28
00:01:59.742 --> 00:02:03.223
She lost her appetite and did not know if it was winter or summer.

29
00:02:04.104 --> 00:02:08.085
Heidi began to look so pale and thin that Sebastian became concerned.

30
00:02:09.826 --> 00:02:12.287
One day, something very mysterious started to happen.

31
00:02:13.347 --> 00:02:15.828
Every morning, the front door was found wide open.

32
00:02:16.809 --> 00:02:19.010
Fraulein could find no explanation for it.

33
00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:24.872
So one night, Sebastian and John, the stable boy, stayed up to watch the front door.

34
00:02:26.528 --> 00:02:32.173
During the night, both men fell asleep, but John suddenly awoke to see a white figure before him.

35
00:02:33.134 --> 00:02:35.435
He gave a cry of alarm and Sebastian woke up.

36
00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:37.357
"What's the matter?

37
00:02:37.817 --> 00:02:38.498
What did you see?"

38
00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:39.919
Sebastian asked.

39
00:02:39.939 --> 00:02:43.502
"A white figure standing on the stairs.

40
00:02:44.443 --> 00:02:47.545
It stood there a minute and disappeared," explained John.

41
00:02:48.606 --> 00:02:50.748
Sebastian felt his blood run cold.

42
00:02:51.869 --> 00:02:55.332
When Fraulein heard the story, she immediately wrote to Clara's father.

43
00:02:56.992 --> 00:03:02.614
When Herr Sesemann read her letter, he did not believe there was a ghost in his house, but

44
00:03:02.854 --> 00:03:04.535
he felt that he should investigate.

45
00:03:05.435 --> 00:03:07.136
Two days later, he arrived at the house.

46
00:03:07.156 --> 00:03:09.937
"And how is the ghost getting on?"

47
00:03:10.377 --> 00:03:12.398
asked Herr Sesemann upon seeing Fraulein.

48
00:03:14.199 --> 00:03:17.700
"It is no joke, I assure you," replied Fraulein.

49
00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:21.422
"You will not laugh tomorrow morning, Herr Sesemann."

50
00:03:22.362 --> 00:03:27.881
Clara's father decided to ask his good friend, Clara's doctor, to come and spend the evening.

51
00:03:29.162 --> 00:03:33.745
The doctor arrived punctually at nine o'clock, and together, they waited up for the ghost.

52
00:03:34.886 --> 00:03:37.147
At one o'clock, there was not a sound in the house.

53
00:03:38.128 --> 00:03:40.410
Then suddenly, the doctor lifted his finger.

54
00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:41.771
They both listened.

55
00:03:43.372 --> 00:03:48.075
They distinctly heard the bar on the door being pushed aside and the key turning in the lock.

56
00:03:49.056 --> 00:03:49.776
"Who is there?"

57
00:03:50.377 --> 00:03:51.237
thundered the doctor.

58
00:03:52.238 --> 00:03:54.940
The figure at the door turned and gave a little cry.

59
00:03:56.033 --> 00:03:59.382
There, standing before them in her white nightgown, was Heidi.
